# Python virtual environment — regenerated on each machine with `python -m venv .venv`.
# Never committed: thousands of files, huge, and every developer's copy is different.
.venv/

# Python bytecode caches — auto-created the first time a module is imported.
# Never committed: purely a performance optimisation, regenerated on demand.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# TODO(you): the app's SQLite database file.
# Hint: plan.md §Section 4 names the exact filename it lives at.
# Reason to ignore: it holds real per-machine data (your cards, your reviews) — not project code.
db.sqlite


# TODO(you): the local secrets file.
# Hint: convention is a dot-prefixed filename that starts with the three letters "env".
#       It doesn't exist yet — we're pre-fencing so we can't ever accidentally commit it.
# Reason to ignore: holds the basic-auth password + any future API keys.
.env


# OS junk — Finder / Windows Explorer scatter these; harmless but noisy in diffs.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor state — per-developer preferences, not part of the project.
.vscode/
.idea/

.pytest_cache/
